{
  "case_id": "2012-11-798",
  "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Supreme Court",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:17 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Trucking Associations, Inc.",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LERMAN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case is about the plain text of the FAAAA express preemption clause and the continuing vitality of this Court's decision in Castle v. Hayes Freight Lines."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: I thought that the Port said we don't apply criminal penalties which come from the tariff, we don't apply those to licensed motor carriers."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Can I break down your arguments into two components, if you might?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Bash, what would you think of this case if the criminal penalties were taken out of it? In other words, if the Port did this all through contract, basically said to each terminal operator, look, if you contract with truckers that don't have this concession agreement, we are going to charge you a higher price."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bash",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BASH: Yes. We think not only is there enough here, but there's another sort of a bright-line rationale before you get into the Boston Harbor sort of understanding of if this is regulatory or market participant. And that's the second factor we cite in our brief, which is we don't consider the Port the equivalent of the cement factory in Reeves, like a commercial enterprise that you might see in the private marketplace."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenthal",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ROSENTHAL: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: At issue today are two provisions contained in a contract between commercial actors. They set forth conditions under which drayage trucks can enter the nonpublic portions of the Port, and they are indistinguishable, indistinguishable from contract provisions that private parties routinely impose on those who seek to enter their property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: You are saying that you can do by contract what you cannot do by regulation. And I don't understand that argument when there are criminal penalties that attach to the breach of the contract."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenthal",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We submit that force and effect of law almost invites a market participant analysis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Rosenthal, could I interrupt you for a second and just make sure I understand what your policy is? Who do you exclude from the Port? What trucks -- what trucks or what trucking companies do you exclude?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenthal",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "trucks that come on to port property sign a nonexclusive concession agreement which agrees to certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "1989711c92c71672c8d649d6577fc3af5082737baa066279973863c52ec7428d",
      "evidence_id": "ev-1989711c92c7-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What -- what if they violate those conditions? I mean, that's -- that's where the -- that's where the shoe pinches."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2012-11-798",
